  "note": "Corrected: a point of V* over an invertible quotient L is an isomorphism L -> O (31232), i.e. a generator of L^∨; so V* = Isom(O_P(1), O_P), which is the torsor of O_P(-1), not O_P(1), for the correspondence L -> Isom(O, L) written on the same board (30903). It is O_P(1) only in the convention L -> Isom(L, O) (EGA's V(L) minus its zero section), which may be what was meant: flagged u.",
